    {
      "text": "thy faith hath made thee whole; go in peace, Mark 5:34. house ye enter, first say, Peace be to this house, Luke 10:5. Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you, John 14:27. in me ye might have peace, John 16:33. saith unto them, Peace be unto you, John 20:19. peace, to every man that worketh good, Rom. 2:10. we have peace with God through our Lord, Rom. 5:1. to be spiritually minded is life and peace, Rom. 8:6. preach the gospel of peace, Rom. 10:15. peace, and joy in the Holy Ghost, Rom. 14:17 (15:13). Grace be unto you, and peace, from God, 1 Cor. 1:3. not the author of confusion, but of peace, 1 Cor. 14:33. fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, Gal. 5:22. he is our peace, Eph. 2:14. feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace, Eph. 6:15. peace of God, which passeth all understanding, Philip. 4:7. let the peace of God rule in your hearts, Col. 3:15. Follow peace … without which no man shall see the Lord, Heb. 12:14. wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, James 3:17. righteousness is sown in peace, James 3:18.",
